1
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:09,740
A visit to the moon.

2
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:15,380
Last month I was lucky enough to have a chance to make a trip into space with my friend Li

3
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:16,800
Yanping, an astronomer.

4
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,880
We visited the moon in our spaceship!

5
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:28,360
Before we left, Li Yanping explained to me that the force of gravity would change three times on our journey

6
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:31,540
and that the first change would be the most powerful.

7
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:33,940
Then we were off.

8
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,740
As the rocket rose into the air,

9
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:42,880
we were pushed back into our seats because we were trying to escape the pull of the earth’s gravity.

10
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:47,820
It was so hard that we could not say anything to each other.

11
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:52,440
Gradually the weight lessened and I was able to talk to him.

12
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:56,080
Why is the spaceship not falling back to the earth?

13
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:02,160
On the earth if I fall from a tree I will fall to the ground." I asked.

14
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:06,780
We are too far from the earth now to feel its pull," he explained, "

15
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:10,460
so we feel as if there is no gravity at all.

16
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:12,620
When we get closer to the moon,

17
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,260
we shall feel its gravity pulling us,

18
00:01:15,260 --> 00:01:21,120
but it will not be as strong a pull as the earth’s." I cheered up immediately

19
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:26,360
and floated weightlessly around in our spaceship cabin watching the earth become smaller

20
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:28,040
and the moon larger.

21
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:32,260
When we got there, I wanted to explore immediately.

22
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:34,200
Come on," I said.

23
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:37,980
If you are right, my mass will be less than on the earth

24
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:41,980
because the moon is smaller and I will be able to move more freely.

25
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:45,960
I might even grow taller if I stay here long enough.

26
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:48,100
I shall certainly weigh less!"

27
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:51,920
I laughed and climbed down the steps from the spaceship.

28
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:54,540
But when I tried to step forward,

29
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:59,320
I found I was carried twice as far as on the earth and fell over.

30
00:02:00,240 --> 00:02:04,560
Oh dear," I cried, "walking does need a bit of practice now

31
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:09,080
that gravity has changed." After a while I got the hang of it

32
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:11,120
and we began to enjoy ourselves.

33
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:16,360
Leaving the moon’s gravity was not as painful as leaving the earth’s.

34
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:19,040
But returning to the earth was very frightening.

35
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:26,680
We watched, amazed as fire broke out on the outside of the spaceship as the earth’s gravity increased.

36
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:32,000
Again we were pushed hard into our seats as we came back to land.

37
00:02:33,300 --> 00:02:37,560
That was very exhausting but very exciting too," I said.

38
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,620
Now I know much more about gravity!

39
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:45,680
Do you think we could visit some stars next time?" "Of course," he smiled, "

40
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,980
which star would you like to go to?
